Wake word models (embedded in the daemon)
  The stop word, echod/internal/feature/detect/assets/stop.tflite — Apache License 2.0
  microWakeWord, https://github.com/kahrendt/microWakeWord. Embedded because it is not a choice:
  nothing selects it and a device without it would have no way to be interrupted.

  The openWakeWord front end, echod/internal/lib/oww/assets/melspectrogram.tflite and
  embedding_model.tflite — Apache License 2.0
  openWakeWord, https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord, whose code is Apache-2.0. The embedding
  model is Google's speech_embedding (https://tfhub.dev/google/speech_embedding/1, Apache-2.0),
  re-implemented by openWakeWord; the melspectrogram model is a fixed-parameter implementation of
  Torch's melspectrogram, not a trained model. openWakeWord's CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 terms cover its six
  pre-trained wake words, which TECHO5 does not ship — the wake words below come from elsewhere.

