Muse client and Bluetooth setup (in the daemon)
  Muse Gadget SDK, Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
  https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk, at commit
  b9008abba7dc4109c66212b9b82e459d08b98b85. These files are ports to Go of the SDK's Linux client
  (linux/src/musegadget), each changed from its source, and each says at its top which SDK file
  it came from and what was changed:
    - echod/internal/lib/muse: api.go, client.go, envelope.go, muse.go, proto.go, session.go and
      turn.go, from muse_api.py, service.py, executor.py, identity.py, config.py, link_client.py
      and noise/ (envelope.py, framing.py, transport.py, _proto.py). session.go and turn.go add
      the chat subscription, reply matching and voice notes, which the Linux client does not have
      and the SDK's ESP32 firmware does (esp32/components/muse).
    - echod/internal/lib/muse/pairing: framing.go, gatt.go, messages.go, network.go, session.go,
      setup.go and verify.go, from ble_framing.py, ble_server.py, identity.py, pairing.py,
      ble_setup.py, network.py, cli.py and muse_api.py.
    - echod/internal/lib/bluez/gatt.go, from ble_server.py.
  The two image settings Muse setup needs, bluetoothd without its battery plugin
  (tools/linux/techo5-lib.sh) and ExchangeMTU = 256 (tools/linux/mkrootfs.sh), follow what the
  SDK's linux/install.sh sets.
  Test vectors, echod/internal/lib/muse/pairing/testdata/link_pairing_v5.json (not shipped in any
  release): copied unchanged from linux/tests/vectors/link_pairing_v5.json. sdk_phone.py beside it
  is this project's own and imports the SDK from a checkout; no SDK code is copied into it.
  The license in full is echod/internal/lib/muse/LICENSE. The SDK ships no NOTICE file.
  Not covered, and not here: Meta says the SDK's Apache license does not cover its default avatar,
  so neither the character nor the code that draws it is in this repository or in any release.
  tools/muse-avatar/make_sprites.py builds the pictures from the user's own SDK checkout.
  TECHO5 is not made or endorsed by Meta. Muse is Meta's.

